<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  doctrine: timebomb-audit

  com.carr.timebomb-audit: weekly scripted time-bomb audit.

  A LAUNCH AGENT, NOT A SCHEDULED MODEL SESSION. PROP-010's ruling
  (see com.carr.calendar-eventkit.plist's own header): deterministic
  recurring work runs from versioned repo code executed by a registered
  Local Edge Node through launchd, not a model session. Scanning tracked
  source for time-bomb signatures, computing deterministic headroom, and
  asking Jev a fixed three-question shape per region is exactly that,
  a predicate pipeline, not a judgement call about what to do next.

  Monday 03:30 local: after nightly-record-layer's 02:05 daily run has long
  finished, well before the working day, and a quiet slot with nothing else
  scheduled at that hour on this machine.

  RISK: YELLOW. Read-only over tracked source and repo history via git;
  sends region snippets (never secrets: ops/typesafe_client.py's own
  credential is read separately and never logged) to Jev for judgment; on
  new findings, writes exactly one record-defect and posts one room-queue
  turn through run.sh call, both already this Mac's normal unattended
  script door (see tools/cutover-watch.py). Never merges, never fixes
  anything itself, never touches the triage ledger.

  See ops/timebomb-audit.py's own header for the full pipeline and
  ops/timebomb-audit-selftest.py for its offline test coverage.

  INSTALLING IT IS A DELIBERATE HUMAN ACT, and there is no installer script on
  purpose: a bin/install-*.sh is an external-admin ingress that would need its
  own SCAC registry successor. From the canonical checkout:
    sed "s|{{REPO}}|$PWD|g" ops/launchd/com.carr.timebomb-audit.plist \
      > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.carr.timebomb-audit.plist
    plutil -lint ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.carr.timebomb-audit.plist
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.carr.timebomb-audit.plist
  Once installed, ops/config-as-code.py check holds the installed body to
  this file like every other CARR LaunchAgent.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.carr.timebomb-audit</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/bin/run-scheduled.sh</string>
    <string>timebomb-audit</string>
    <string>launchd.run</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/.venv/bin/python</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/ops/timebomb-audit.py</string>
  </array>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/opt/homebrew/opt/libpq/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
    <key>CARR_REPO</key>
    <string>{{REPO}}</string>
  </dict>

  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>3</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>{{REPO}}/out/timebomb-audit.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>{{REPO}}/out/timebomb-audit.log</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
